**Not implemented / simplified relative to the spec:**

- Challenging-stage enemies use simple looping waypoint paths (arcs/U-loops) rather than the arcade's exact figure-8 patterns, and wave-bonus/PERFECT text is shown on the results screen rather than as a dedicated in-stage screen.
- Boss tractor-beam capture requires the player to be roughly under the beam at its widest; the arcade's precise beam-collision timing is approximated.
- Enemy dive paths are single quadratic Béziers (out, then back to slot) rather than the multi-segment looping arcs of the original; escorts follow the Boss as a fixed offset.
- The "captive turns hostile" case (Boss killed in formation) simply destroys the fighter with an explosion, as the spec's "does not return" allows.
- Extra-ship award caps reserves at 6 icons; the arcade's exact 1UP/2UP credit handling and coin-insert flow is omitted (single player only).
- Sound effects are short synthesized approximations of the arcade's melodies (e.g., the stage jingle is a 4-note arpeggio, not the full tune).
